        "title": "Beautiful Hindu Temple.",
        "text": "I keep visiting this place with my tour groups. A nice place to know about Hindu culture. But makes me a bit sad.. Not by looking at cremation but things happening around. Lot of tourist take photos of cremation which is a disrespect to the local culture and family who lost their loved one. Its not entertainment. Tourist are allowed here so that they can know more about the culture and tradition... Lot of hawkers who keep walking around u trying to sell stuff.. Authorities should come up with ideas of keeping the Bagmati river(temple is on bank of this river) more clean so that it doesn't get polluted. Ppl dump many other trash else then ashes in river, this is not good. They need to work on it..\nIt is lovely place to learn more about Hindu culture n traditions followed in Nepal. Few Sadhus are around here who want to get clicked and will charge u for it. So if u want a good shot, pay them a little bit n get it. Non Hindus are not allowed in main temple area but can walk around other parts of temple area. It have a entry fee of 1000NPR for foreigners. ",
