      {
        "review_id": 479983634,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r479983634-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "An absolute must while in Kathmandu",
        "text": "This was by far the most interesting sight in Kathmandu.  This temple is dedicated to Shiva and is fronted by a huge terrace where there is a warren of activity.  You will find cows and calves strolling, packs of monkeys running around, flocks of birds, throngs of barefoot Hindus coming to warship, lepers and the sick sleeping or begging for money at the edges of the entrance, sadhus (ascetic, Hindu monk-like characters) sitting around or making money from tourist photos.  The sights and sounds here are thrilling.  Only Hindus are allowed to enter the temple but once you walk across the bridge to the other side of the river, you can get a great view of the golden center of the temple as well as the crematoria below the temple, along the horribly polluted river.  The bank of the river opposite the temple is beautiful, with small shrines containing lingam/uni statues lined arranged in linear patterns that produce beautiful imagery.  Sadhus were sitting around and chatting, waiting to make money from tourists snapping photos of them.",
